  "verbalization": "Ixoside is shown to have a direct target relationship with RWLeu4 through multiple pathways, with the most consistent evidence linking Ixoside to RWLeu4 via the compound (1S,3R,6S,8R,11S,12S,15R,16R)-15-[(2R)-4-[(2R)-3,3-dimethyloxiran-2-yl]butan-2-yl]-7,7,12,16-tetramethylpentacyclo[9.7.0.01,3.03,8.012,16]octadecan-6-ol. This compound is identified as a target of Ixoside and also as a target of MIP and Quercetagetin 3-methyl ether 7-glucoside, which further supports the pathway to RWLeu4. The evidence suggests that Ixoside may act through a mechanism involving the inhibition or modulation of a target enzyme or protein that is involved in the biosynthesis or function of the mentioned compound, which in turn affects RWLeu4. The presence of multiple overlapping targets and the consistent pathway across different evidence scores indicate a plausible mechanistic link between Ixoside and RWLeu4, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
